config ZMK_KSCAN_GPIO_DUPLEX
    bool "Japanese duplex matrix keyboard scan driver"
    depends on GPIO
    select KSCAN
    help
      Enable support for Japanese duplex matrix scanning.

      This driver allows bidirectional scanning of a keyboard matrix,
      where the same GPIO pins alternate between column (output) and
      row (input) roles in two separate scanning passes.

      This significantly reduces the number of GPIO pins needed:
      - Standard 4x13 matrix: 17 pins
      - Duplex 7+4 matrix: 11 pins (52+ keys capacity)

      Requires proper diode placement for bidirectional scanning.
